#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22e654fb-0cb3-564f-859e-684bc6ac3a2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360252} {:answer/id #uuid "9bd909b0-e213-5170-b17b-3edd5fa6d5f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360253} {:answer/id #uuid "bf82c987-3676-5344-9c1a-476ad9c51d48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360254} {:answer/id #uuid "302061b9-bb5b-5632-8951-c1bcffce9658" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360255} {:answer/id #uuid "eaab32b5-fb09-51f9-bb95-840e486945ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "302061b9-bb5b-5632-8951-c1bcffce9658" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360255} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e8303ce-a136-5edf-b143-3b65f3d1283c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "308a128f-c3b5-54e4-a46d-fbae8dd63c97" :question/math-academy-id "q-149564" :question/problem "| **Number of Members ($x$)** | $3$ | $4$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Number of Cars ($y$)** | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ | $6$ |\n\nIn a survey of $4$ families, the number of members in each family was recorded as well as the number of cars owned by that family. The data is shown in the table above.\nCompute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=4$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(3-4)(2-3)+(4-4)(2-3)+(4-4)(2-3)+(5-4)(6-3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-1)(-1)+(0)(-1)+(0)(-1)+(1)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[1+0+0+3] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72c61957-55ea-58cf-9273-4522b3f8a072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360259} {:answer/id #uuid "27ef66a0-b9ad-58ac-bb9f-b29c9fc5750d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360260} {:answer/id #uuid "4a18b879-4571-552b-9fa9-f88a0eef33e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360261} {:answer/id #uuid "251ebd13-d55b-500c-a810-b1367a01e8dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360262} {:answer/id #uuid "5d132bed-0864-5d61-a97e-e36d677d924c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72c61957-55ea-58cf-9273-4522b3f8a072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360259} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6132d06-c0d4-5b9e-9c45-e4dfa26c7569" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aedf8fc3-dbed-5730-9f21-b8c81e10ed3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-149570" :question/problem "| **Years in the 1st division ($x$)** | $44$ | $38$ | $32$ | $30$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Number of Championships ($y$)** | $4$ | $3$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n\nThe table above shows the number of years four English soccer teams have been in the top division and the number of national championships they have won. \nCompute the covariance of the data sets." :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (44+38+32+30) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 144 \\\\  & =36 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (4+3+3+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(44\\,-\\,36)(4\\,-\\,4)+(38\\,-\\,36)(3\\,-\\,4)+(32\\,-\\,36)(3\\,-\\,4)+(30\\,-\\,36)(6\\,-\\,4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(8)(0)+(2)(-1)+(-4)(-1)+(-6)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+(-2)+4+(-12)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-10) \\\\  & =-2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360264 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f7bf132-19c3-5728-baf1-0206f165253f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360266} {:answer/id #uuid "926e08ff-1e28-5eb1-a9fc-9ae46a37b025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360267} {:answer/id #uuid "ea953bc3-2546-5c6c-819c-fc01fa27e7f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360268} {:answer/id #uuid "40448e8f-a346-5f96-a96a-524ab41d2e54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360269} {:answer/id #uuid "9731e646-5540-52b7-aadd-63a8f615fde4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea953bc3-2546-5c6c-819c-fc01fa27e7f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360268} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9b32f33-1de9-5d68-bec4-966608b18422" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ac2ef26-e44c-5f13-aaa3-d7e817fbe704" :question/math-academy-id "q-149571" :question/problem "| **Year of Experience, in years ($x$)** | $1$ | $2$ | $2$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Number of Strikes ($y$)** | $2$ | $1$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n\nFour friends went bowling. The table above shows their years of bowling experience and the number of strikes they got in the game.\nCompute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=3$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(1-3)(2-3)+(2-3)(1-3)+(2-3)(3-3)+(7-3)(6-3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-2)(-1)+(-1)(-2)+(-1)(0)+(4)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[2+2+0+12] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f49453e-af01-583e-8901-3233c603996f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360273} {:answer/id #uuid "1007fd83-8622-5480-a412-692af3da29a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360274} {:answer/id #uuid "18724f14-7f52-586e-827c-7cb399c2c942" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360275} {:answer/id #uuid "58b70067-7d87-53fc-9414-708d983a08e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360276} {:answer/id #uuid "e924e357-dd18-50d8-a41e-f1718ead1747" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1007fd83-8622-5480-a412-692af3da29a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360274} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a0c7361-5f4e-5202-a29f-f5bce3a55eeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c0b0103-1c88-5cc9-84a1-93f9985616e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-149617" :question/problem "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={6,\\,4,\\,8,\\,6},\\,y={4,\\,7,\\,11,\\,14}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=9.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(6-6)(4-9)+(4-6)(7-9)+(8-6)(11-9)+(6-6)(14-9)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(0)(-5)+(-2)(-2)+(2)(2)+(0)(5)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+4+4+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29923786-ad5b-56f9-a146-0a084c09261f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360280} {:answer/id #uuid "8393a22a-eb45-5d8f-9255-47aed91de351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360281} {:answer/id #uuid "d90d32bd-093d-5e5f-90f7-4a91e39b2fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360282} {:answer/id #uuid "e49fb562-c40b-522c-9967-30b74e5f3889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360283} {:answer/id #uuid "da956414-cb57-59a4-aa82-33a2a4cc1d25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8393a22a-eb45-5d8f-9255-47aed91de351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360281} :answer-field/id #uuid "4367bed7-7046-573e-9881-1ac34861d477" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23453827-8519-5d16-8adc-b4ba457a8582" :question/math-academy-id "q-149618" :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y)$ for the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={-12,\\,-10,\\,-9,\\,-13},\\,y={-2,\\,0,\\,3,\\,3}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-12-10-9-13) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-44) \\\\  & =-11 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-2+0+3+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-12-(-11))(-2-1)+(-10-(-11))(0-1) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+(-9-(-11))(3-1)+(-13-(-11))(3-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-1)(-3)+(1)(-1)+(2)(2)+(-2)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[3-1+4-4] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
